## Why This Is Asked

Temporal-like constraints on feature flags across release cycles test three-valued propagation and branching heuristics—skills essential for configuration validation at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued logic with implication defined as ¬A ∨ B
- Propagation rules for ¬, ∨, ∧, and →
- Backtracking search treating U as a first-class domain value

## Code Example

```javascript
// Three-valued backtracking propagator sketch
const VALUES = { T: 2, U: 1, F: 0 };
const NOT = { T: 'F', F: 'T', U: 'U' };
const OR = (a, b) => VALUES[a] >= VALUES[b] ? a : b;
const AND = (a, b) => VALUES[a] <= VALUES[b] ? a : b;
const IMPLIES = (a, b) => OR(NOT[a], b);

function propagate(constraints, assignment) {
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [ante, conseq] of constraints) {
      const a = assignment[ante], c = assignment[conseq];
      if (a === 'F' && c !== 'F') { assignment[conseq] = 'F'; changed = true; }
      if (a === 'T' && c !== 'T') { assignment[conseq] = 'T'; changed = true; }
      if (c === 'F' && a !== 'F') { assignment[ante] = 'F'; changed = true; }
    }
  }
  return assignment;
}
```

